From 14a77da8224ea958226a04dcf2b771a48e04d220 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 05:57:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] retain and reconcile evicted scratch custody safely

Keep host-local path custody separate from synced task ownership. Recover legacy custody only from an exact original admission/session/run-tombstone link; require fresh terminal Board evidence, existing retention, archive guards, and unchanged local task/receipt fence before rename.

Proof: canonical 8-file suite 306 passed; 84 original safety mutants killed plus 36 reliability mutants killed (overlapping reruns). Read-only replay across 10 boards and 10 sync shadows, 8127 admissions: zero current legacy recovery matches, three foreign-tree sessions rejected; no cross-board managed-path overlaps. Worker target provenance verified separately from original local run8815 admission/session cwd and tombstone; deployment and natural timer proof pending.
